Privacy Policy for Feline Fitness
Last Updated: October 27, 2026

Your privacy is important to us. This policy explains how the Feline Fitness application handles information.

Information We Use
Feline Fitness is designed to operate without collecting, storing, or transmitting any of your personal information off your device. We believe in privacy by design.

Device Permissions
To function properly, the app requires specific device permissions. These are used exclusively for the following local purposes:

Bluetooth & Location: The app requires permission to access your device's Bluetooth and Location services. This is used solely to scan for, connect to, and communicate with the Feline Fitness hardware. On some operating systems, location permission is required to perform Bluetooth scans.

Camera & Photo Library: To personalize your cat profiles, the app requests access to your device's camera or photo library. This allows you to set custom profile pictures for your pets.

Data Storage & Security
All data generated or used by the app—including custom toy names, cat profiles, profile photos, and activity history—is stored entirely locally on your device. None of this data, including your photos, is ever transmitted to external servers, collected by us, or shared with any third party.

Changes to This Policy
We may update our Privacy Policy from time to time. We will notify you of any changes by posting the new Privacy Policy on this page.

